# Old urls, one line per move. Cloudflare reads this file from the output root; Jekyll copies it because
# _config.yml names it under include:. A closed line renders under the highest version it shipped, so a folder
# rename moves urls once and never again.
#
# 302 while the moves are being checked - a browser caches a 301 and a wrong one cannot be taken back. They
# become 301 once every line has been checked on the deployed site.
#
# Exact lines before the wildcard they would otherwise fall under.
/version/v3.0.x/swagger/v3.html   /swagger/v3/                  302
/version/v3.0.x/swagger/v4.html   /swagger/v4/                  302
/version/v3.0.x/*                 /:splat                       302
/version/latest/*                 /:splat                       302
/version/v2.1.x/swagger/v2.html   /version/2.1.1/swagger/v2/    302
/version/v2.1.x/swagger/v3.html   /version/2.1.1/swagger/v3/    302
/version/v2.1.x/*                 /version/2.1.1/:splat         302
/version/v2.0.x/*                 /version/2.1.1/:splat         302
/version/v1.3.x/swagger/v1.html   /version/1.3.0/swagger/v1/    302
/version/v1.3.x/swagger/v2.html   /version/1.3.0/swagger/v2/    302
/version/v1.3.x/swagger/v3.html   /version/1.3.0/swagger/v3/    302
/version/v1.3.x/*                 /version/1.3.0/:splat         302

